# Language Conventions

> **Rule**: ALL code, documentation, and comments MUST be in English

## Code Language

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: English everywhere
const appointmentDate = new Date();
const isAvailable = checkAvailability(slot);
function handleBookingSubmit() { /* ... */ }

// ❌ BAD: Other languages in code
const fechaCita = new Date();
const estaDisponible = verificarDisponibilidad(slot);
function manejarEnvioReserva() { /* ... */ }
```

## Variable and Function Names

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
const professionalList = [];
const userProfile = {};
function calculateTotalPrice() {}
function validateAppointment() {}

// ❌ BAD
const listaProfesionales = [];
const perfilUsuario = {};
function calcularPrecioTotal() {}
function validarCita() {}
```

## Comments

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: English comments
// Check if the slot is available before booking
// This handles the edge case where...

// ❌ BAD: Non-English comments
// Verificar si el slot está disponible
// Esto maneja el caso especial donde...
```

## Error Messages and UI Text

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: English in code, i18n for user-facing text
throw new Error('Invalid appointment date');
console.error('Failed to fetch professionals');

// For user-facing text, use translation keys
const ERROR_MESSAGES = {
  INVALID_DATE: 'Invalid appointment date',
  FETCH_FAILED: 'Failed to load data',
};
```

## Documentation

```tsx
/**
 * ✅ GOOD: JSDoc in English
 * Fetches available time slots for a professional
 * @param professionalId - The professional's unique identifier
 * @returns Array of available time slots
 */
function getAvailableSlots(professionalId: string) {}

/**
 * ❌ BAD: JSDoc in other language
 * Obtiene los horarios disponibles para un profesional
 * @param idProfesional - Identificador único del profesional
 */
```

## File and Folder Names

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
features/appointments/
components/BookingCard.tsx
hooks/useAvailability.ts
shared/dtos/professional.dto.ts

// ❌ BAD
features/citas/
components/TarjetaReserva.tsx
hooks/useDisponibilidad.ts
shared/dtos/profesional.dto.ts
```

## Git Commits

```bash
# ✅ GOOD
git commit -m "feat: add appointment booking flow"
git commit -m "fix: resolve availability slot overlap"

# ❌ BAD
git commit -m "feat: agregar flujo de reserva de citas"
```

## Why English?

1. **Industry standard** - Most libraries, docs, and resources are in English
2. **Team collaboration** - Enables working with international teams
3. **Code consistency** - Mixing languages creates cognitive overhead
4. **Tooling support** - Better autocomplete, linting, and AI assistance
